      "thm:weighted-cycle-space"
    ],
    "justification": "Attainment turns the information bound into an implementable precision correction based only on cohort means and within-cohort covariances.",
    "gap": "Roth and Sant'Anna (2023, Proposition 2.1) optimize design-based additive estimators within a class; this result attains the superpopulation semiparametric bound for a nonlinear proportional target.",
    "consumer": "Applied users obtain an analytic alternative to unit-bootstrap inference for the cohort-mean PPML benchmark in fixed-horizon panels.",
    "proof_tex": "The PPML coefficient is feasible for the target gradient. Indeed, using the definitions of \\(S\\) and \\(h_{\\mathrm{CM}}\\), and commutativity of \\(M\\) and \\(P_U\\),\n\\[\nJ^{\\prime}h_{\\mathrm{CM}}\n=\\begin{pmatrix}X^{\\prime}MP_UXS^{-1}c_\\beta\\\\c_D\\end{pmatrix}\n=\\begin{pmatrix}c_\\beta\\\\c_D\\end{pmatrix}\n=c.                                                      \\tag{1}\n\\]\nEvery other solution of \\(J^{\\prime}h=c\\) is \\(h_{\\mathrm{CM}}+R\\gamma\\). Since \\(K=R^{\\prime}\\Omega R\\succ0\\),\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n(h_{\\mathrm{CM}}+R\\gamma)^{\\prime}\\Omega(h_{\\mathrm{CM}}+R\\gamma)\n&=h_{\\mathrm{CM}}^{\\prime}\\Omega h_{\\mathrm{CM}}\n-b_{\\mathrm{cyc}}^{\\prime}K^{-1}b_{\\mathrm{cyc}}\\\\\n&\\quad+\n(\\gamma+K^{-1}b_{\\mathrm{cyc}})^{\\prime}\nK(\\gamma+K^{-1}b_{\\mathrm{cyc}}).\n\\end{aligned}                                           \\tag{2}\n\\]\nThus the unique minimum is attained by\n\\[\nh_{\\mathrm{CM}}-RK^{-1}b_{\\mathrm{cyc}}.                \\tag{3}\n\\]\nLagrange minimization of \\(h^{\\prime}\\Omega h\\) subject to \\(J^{\\prime}h=c\\) gives \\(\\Omega^{-1}J(J^{\\prime}\\Omega^{-1}J)^{-1}c=h^{\\star}\\). Hence (3) equals \\(h^{\\star}\\). For \\(q=0\\), the same conclusion holds with empty cycle matrices.\n\nThe consistency results in the PPML proof and continuity give, on events with probability tending to one,\n\\[\n\\widehat R\\to_PR,\\quad\n\\widehat\\Omega\\to_P\\Omega,\\quad\n\\widehat h_{\\mathrm{CM}}\\to_Ph_{\\mathrm{CM}},\\quad\n\\widehat b_{\\mathrm{cyc}}\\to_Pb_{\\mathrm{cyc}},\\quad\n\\widehat K\\to_PK.                                       \\tag{4}\n\\]\nFor a fundamental cycle \\(e=(g,t)\\), the population log contrast is zero because \\(\\mu_{gt}=a_gb_t\\). Positivity of its four cell means permits Taylor expansion:\n\\[\n\\sqrt N\\widehat\\kappa\n=R^{\\prime}\\sqrt N(\\overline Y-m)+o_P(1).               \\tag{5}\n\\]\nCombining the PPML expansion with (4)--(5), and using \\(\\widehat\\kappa=O_P(N^{-1/2})\\), gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt N(\\widehat\\theta_{\\mathrm{eff}}-\\theta_{\\mathrm{PTT}})\n&=\\{h_{\\mathrm{CM}}-RK^{-1}b_{\\mathrm{cyc}}\\}^{\\prime}\n\\sqrt N(\\overline Y-m)+o_P(1)\\\\\n&=h^{\\star\\prime}\\sqrt N(\\overline Y-m)+o_P(1).\n\\end{aligned}                                           \\tag{6}\n\\]\nThe fallback on \\(\\mathcal E_N^c\\) is irrelevant because \\(\\Pr(\\mathcal E_N^c)\\to0\\). Moreover,\n\\[\nh^{\\star\\prime}\\sqrt N(\\overline Y-m)\n=N^{-1/2}\\sum_{g\\in C}\\sum_{i=1}^{n_g}\n\\frac{h_g^{\\star\\prime}(Y_{gi}-m_g)}{p_g}+o_P(1),        \\tag{7}\n\\]\nwhere replacing \\(n_g/N\\) by \\(p_g\\) costs \\(o_P(1)\\). The summand is the stratified representation of \\(\\phi^{\\star}\\). The fixed-strata central limit theorem gives variance \\(h^{\\star\\prime}\\Omega h^{\\star}=V^{\\star}\\), which the canonical-gradient theorem identifies as the lower bound. Thus the feasible estimator attains \\(V^{\\star}\\) pointwise.",
